*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Write the time-independent Schrödinger equation in the different regions of the potential well.

2. Apply boundary conditions at the interfaces: the wavefunction $psi(x)$ and its derivative $psi'(x)$ must be continuous (except at infinite barriers where $psi(x) = 0$).

3. Match the solutions at the boundaries to set up a system of linear equations for the coefficients.

4. Set the determinant of the coefficients system to zero to obtain the transcendental equation for the allowed energy states.
